\alttext(The printed bias and variance sum to latent prediction error for every fitted degree.)


> Conclusion

The quadratic example verifies the basis transformation. Across noisy replicas the bias–variance
identity holds numerically, and training error alone does not describe latent prediction risk.
These are conditional results at a fixed design and noise level; selecting degree needs separate validation.

> References

- [NIST DLMF: Legendre recurrence](https://dlmf.nist.gov/18.9).
- [Hastie, Tibshirani and Friedman: The Elements of Statistical Learning, chapter 7](https://hastie.su.domains/ElemStatLearn/).
